  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 32,
    "summary": "Elihu, in anger, answers Job and his three friends—Elihu says, There is a spirit in man, and the inspiration of the Almighty gives understanding—He also says, Great men are not always wise.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "So these three men ceased to answer Job, because he was righteous in his own eyes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 32:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Then was kindled the wrath of Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite, of the kindred of Ram: against Job was his wrath kindled, because he justified himself rather than God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 32:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Also against his three friends was his wrath kindled, because they had found no answer, and yet had condemned Job.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 95
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 32:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Now Elihu had waited till Job had spoken, because they were elder than he.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 32:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "When Elihu saw that there was no answer in the mouth of these three men, then his wrath was kindled.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 29
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 32:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite answered and said, I am young, and ye are very old; wherefore I was afraid, and durst not shew you mine opinion.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 64
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 32:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "I said, Days should speak, and multitude of years should teach wisdom.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 32:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 7
      },
